/-- p25025 — 25:F3. Quotation exceeds mention: a formula's arity is below its length. No sentence $\lambda$ contains a subformula whose truth depends on all coordinates of a tuple of arity at least $\lvert \lambda\rvert$. Under any coding that spends at least $\lvert \lambda\rvert$ coordinates on $\lambda$, per-symbol coding included, no sentence's truth is sensitive to every coordinate of its own code. -/
theorem p25025 : (∀ (φ : FRC.Diagonal.Fm) (j N : Nat), (∀ (i : Nat), i < N → FRC.Diagonal.occ (i + j) φ = true) → N < FRC.Diagonal.size φ) ∧ (∀ (p : Nat) (φ : FRC.Diagonal.Fm) (j N : Nat), (∀ (i : Nat), i < N → ∃ env v, FRC.Diagonal.holds p (FRC.Diagonal.upd env (i + j) v) φ ≠ FRC.Diagonal.holds p env φ) → N < FRC.Diagonal.size φ) ∧ ∀ (p : Nat) {ψ lam : FRC.Diagonal.Fm}, FRC.Diagonal.Subformula ψ lam → ∀ (j N : Nat), FRC.Diagonal.size lam ≤ N → ¬∀ (i : Nat), i < N → ∃ env v, FRC.Diagonal.holds p (FRC.Diagonal.upd env (i + j) v) ψ ≠ FRC.Diagonal.holds p env ψ :=
  And.intro @FRC.Diagonal.arity_lt_size (And.intro @FRC.Diagonal.mention_cost_lt (@FRC.Diagonal.no_self_reading))
